# Production ECS Architecture

Target: mature, extensible DOTS architecture for a large AA city-survival sim.

## Layers

```
Main: Startup / composition root only
Presentation (UI, camera, FMOD, Shell FSM, save file)
  → desired fields or one-shot requests, no economy math
Simulation (ECS): source of truth
Content: Authoring/Baker, blobs, prefabs, balance tables
```

Assemblies are compile walls, not DDD layers. Simulation, Content (art catalogs), Authoring, Presentation, Main. See wiki `01 Folder Structure`. Simulation does not reference Content.

## Simulation folders (feature, then layer)

`Simulation/<Feature>/{Components,Commands,CommandSystems,Systems}`  
Tick: Commands → commute/construction → production → day clock. Needs/Laws/Gods/WinLose later.

## Rules

- One write model: ECS simulation world
- Systems = domain rules; components = state; avoid rich OO aggregates on entities
- Two writes from the player. **Desired state** is a field on an entity the player already has (`Workplace.DesiredWorkers`, building pause, a feed rate): the UI sets it, the next system reconciles the world to it. **One-shot actions** stay requests (`SimCommands` / a request entity): place, demolish, spawn, pay, clock, ritual. They change structure or must land in order on the tick.
- UI does not write outcomes: stocks, loyalty, positions, `WorkingCount`. A button may read to grey itself. The clamp lives in the system.
- Singletons for global state (`GameTime`, `SimControl`, ledgers) — not VContainer in core
- DI only optional in Presentation (UI, FMOD, save)
- ScriptableObjects/authoring = design-time; runtime truth = entities
- Workers are **agents** with assignment and commute; pathfinding later
- Production scales with `WorkingCount / WorkplaceSlots` (recipe is the 100% rate)
- Every resource has a stock cap derived from buildings (warehouses / energy grants). See `economy-stock-cap`
- Prefer data-driven content for new buildings/resources/laws

## Anti-patterns

- `Button.onClick` computing production
- God `IEconomyService` used by UI and systems alike
- Mixing jam card architecture into ECS core
- Burst systems calling managed UI/FMOD directly
- `Time.timeScale` as city pause
